id: 43
hanzi: 交给
pinyin: jiāo gěi
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to hand over; to entrust; to deliver to
  es: entregar; poner en manos de; confiar a

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to transfer physical custody, possession, responsibility, or authority into someone's hands | entregar; encomendar; poner en manos o custodia de otra persona | 交给父母 (hand over to parents)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 子路一进家门，便迫不及待地将装满百斤白米的大口袋稳稳交给了倚在床头的双亲。 | Zǐlù yí jìn jiāmén, biàn pòbùjídài de jiāng zhuāngmǎn bǎijīn báimǐ de dà kǒudài wěnwěn jiāogěi le yǐ zài chuángtóu de shuāngqīn. | The moment Zilu crossed the threshold, he eagerly handed over the heavy sack of white rice securely to his parents resting on the bed. | En cuanto Zilu cruzó el umbral, entregó con premura y firmeza el pesado saco de arroz a sus padres que reposaban en la cama.
  #2 | 项目经理在例会上郑重决定，将下一季度核心算法架构优化的重任交给出色的青年骨干团队。 | Xiàngmù jīnglǐ zài lìhuì shàng zhèngzhòng juédìng, jiāng xià yí jìdù héxīn suànfǎ jiàgòu yōuhuà de zhòngrèn jiāogěi chūsè de qīngnián gǔgàn tuánduì. | At the regular meeting, the project manager solemnly decided to entrust next quarter's core algorithm optimization to the outstanding young backbone team. | En la reunión regular, el director de proyecto decidió solemnemente confiar la optimización del algoritmo central del próximo trimestre al sobresaliente equipo de jóvenes líderes.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  交给父母 | hand over to parents
  交给老师 | hand over to the teacher
  任务交给 | assign the task to
  交给警方 | hand over to the police
  权力交给 | transfer power to
  全权交给 | entrust full authority to

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  物归原主 | wù guī yuán zhǔ | return property to its rightful owner
  移花接木 | yí huā jiē mù | surreptitiously substitute one thing for another
  付诸东流 | fù zhū dōng liú | all efforts cast into the eastward river (wasted)
  授人以渔 | shòu rén yǐ yú | give a person a fishhook; teach someone how to fish

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  交 | jiāo | cross; intersect; exchange; deliver | cruzar; intercambiar; entregar | 亠 | lid / head | 亠 (head) + 父-like crossed legs | 交 (original crossed lines) | 6 | 上下结构 | Pictogram of a person standing with legs crossed in an exchange or meeting, developing into handing over or mutual interaction. | A figure crossing paths to hand over and exchange goods. | Una persona que cruza sus pasos para entregar e intercambiar pertenencias. | 55 | YK | ""
  给 | gěi | give; grant; provide | dar; otorgar; conceder | 纟 | silk / thread | 纟 (silk cords bound together) | 合 (hé / together / join phonetic) | 9 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: 纟 (silk cord tying a package) + 合 (fitting together), meaning to supply, equip, or pass along tightly bound supplies. | Tying silk threads (纟) around provisions to fit together (合) and give them to someone in need. | Atar hilos de seda (纟) a los víveres para que encajen (合) y dárselos al necesitado. | 214 | VFOR | 給

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Crossing paths (交) to deliver tightly bound provisions (给) means to hand over and entrust (交给).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Salir al cruce (交) para entregar un atadillo de seda (给) simboliza entregar en propias manos (交给).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In Confucian filial piety, the solemn act of 交给 symbolizes not merely handing over material food, but delivering one's filial devotion, loyalty, and heart to one's lineage.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone followed by a 3rd tone dipped low: jiāo gěi (55-214).

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    文 | wén | culture; script | Lacks the lower crossed legs strokes of 交
    父 | fù | father | Has crossing strokes at bottom without the top lid stroke 亠
    绘 | huì | paint; draw | Has 会 (huì) on the right of 纟 instead of 合
    络 | luò | net; web | Has 各 on the right of 纟 instead of 合
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    交付 | jiāo fù | deliver; hand over payment
    交谈 | jiāo tán | converse; chat
    给予 | jǐ yǔ | grant; bestow
    供应 | gōng yìng | supply; provide

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 交给 emphasizes transferring custody, physical possession, or moral responsibility from one party into the direct care of another.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 交给 vs. 递给 | dìgěi | 交给 emphasizes the shift of ownership, duty, or custody, whereas 递给 focuses strictly on the physical motion of extending one's arm to pass an item.
    2 | 交给 vs. 付给 | fùgěi | 交给 applies broadly to goods, duties, and trust, whereas 付给 is restricted to monetary payment and compensation.
    3 | 交给 vs. 送给 | sònggěi | 交给 implies an obligation, duty, or returning of custody, whereas 送给 denotes a voluntary gift or generous donation.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 子路顶着刺骨风雪将白米背回家中。他顾不上拍去肩头厚厚的积雪，恭敬地将米袋和碎银子全部交给了双亲。老母亲抚摸着他冻僵的双手，满含热泪地笑了。 | Zǐlù dǐngzhe cìgǔ fēngxuě jiāng báimǐ bēi huí jiāzhōng. Tā gùbushàng pāi qù jiāntóu hòuhòu de jīxuě, gōngjìng de jiāng mǐdài hé suìyínzi quánbù jiāogěi le shuāngqīn. Lǎo mǔqīn fǔmōzhe tā dòngjiāng de shuāngshǒu, mǎnhán rèlèi de xiào le. | Braving the freezing snowstorm, Zilu carried the rice home. Without even brushing snow from his shoulders, he respectfully handed the rice sack and silver to his parents. His mother caressed his frozen hands and smiled through tears. | Desafiando la gélida ventisca, Zilu cargó el arroz hasta casa. Sin sacudirse la nieve, entregó respetuosamente el saco y las monedas a sus padres. Su anciana madre acarició sus manos congeladas y sonrió entre lágrimas.
  #2 | 在现代软件工程与敏捷研发流程中，系统集成测试完毕后，开发团队必须按照严格的标准将稳定版本和详尽的运维文档正式交给出海支持团队。明确的交接界面不仅有助于各部门厘清权责，更能最大限度地降低生产环境出现重大技术故障的潜在风险。 | Zài xiàndài ruǎnjiàn gōngchéng yǔ mǐnjié yánfā liúchéng zhōng, xìtǒng jíchéng cèshì wánbì hòu, kāifā tuánduì bìxū ànzhào yángé de biāozhǔn jiāng wěndìng bǎnběn yǔ xiángjìn de yùnwéi wéndàng zhèngshì jiāogěi chūhǎi zhīchí tuánduì. Míngquè de jiāojiē jièmiàn bùjǐn yǒuzhùyú gè bùmén líqīng quánzé, gèng néng zuìdà xiàndù de jiàngdī shēngchǎn huánjìng chūxiàn zhòngdà jìshù gùzhàng de qiánzài fēngxiǎn. | In modern software engineering and agile development, after integration testing, developers must officially hand over the stable build and documentation to operations. A clear handover interface clarifies responsibilities across teams and minimizes the risk of production failure. | En la ingeniería de software moderna y las metodologías ágiles, el equipo de desarrollo debe entregar oficialmente la versión estable y la documentación técnica al equipo de operaciones. Delimitar con rigor esta entrega define responsabilidades y previene fallos críticos en producción.
